From c785bdd6f544ff1b88a6d4aafb6b643be12fb635 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andras Timar <andras.timar@collabora.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:59:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] write gradients of more than two colours as loext gradient
 stops

A gradient given as svg:linearGradient or svg:radialGradient became a
two-colour draw:gradient from the vector's first two stops, whatever
their number: a gradient of three colours lost its last one, and its
start was the middle colour.

draw:start-color (and draw:start of the opacity) is now the last stop
and draw:end-color the first one, as it already was for two stops, and
when these two cannot express the gradient (more than two stops, or a
stop inside the gradient) its stops are written as
<loext:gradient-stop> children of draw:gradient and <loext:opacity-stop>
children of draw:opacity. Their offsets follow the existing order: a
stop at svg:offset x is at 1 - x, from draw:start-color. Documents with
two stops at 0 and 1 are written as before, apart from the loext
namespace, now declared by the ODG, ODP, ODS and ODT generators.
---
